.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Home Assistant URL and long-lived token for the hardware session.
.env

# Raw capture journal, and the previous runs rotated aside beside it. Frames
# worth keeping are promoted into the protocol document as Pronto blocks by
# `tools/hw.py pronto`; the rest is session noise.
tests/hardware/journal.jsonl
tests/hardware/journal.*.jsonl

# What a human read off the appliance's panel during one session. Kept only so
# stopping a session part-way does not lose the answers already given: an answer
# is not a durable fact about the appliance, it is a fact about one session, and
# the same test has produced contradictory answers depending only on where the
# emitter sat. The conclusions live in docs/ha_ir_platform/plan.md.
tests/hardware/answers.toml
